us.github.io/post/2024-10-15-latent-reasoning-traces/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-10-15-latent-reasoning-traces/</guid><description>What if LLMs could remember their own successful reasoning? A simple experiment in trace retrieval, and why &amp;#39;latent&amp;#39; is the right word.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-10-15-latent-reasoning-traces/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">LLM</media:title></media:content><category>machine-learning</category><category>LLM</category><category>bayesian-inference</category><category>reasoning</category><category>retrieval</category><category>case-based-reasoning</category></item><item><title>Neural Language Models: From RNNs to Transformers</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-20-neural-language-models-transformers/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-20-neural-language-models-transformers/</guid><description>The evolution of neural sequence prediction, and how it connects to classical methods</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-20-neural-language-models-transformers/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">LLM</media:title></media:content><category>sequential-prediction</category><category>neural-networks</category><category>transformers</category><category>language-models</category><category>attention</category><category>gpt</category><category>llm</category></item><item><title>A Home Lab from Spare Parts</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/diy-home-lab/</link><pubDate>Sat, 10 Jun 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/diy-home-lab/</guid><description>I built a home lab from spare 